On x86 you can monitor writes to cachelines. Its really used by the idle thread on OS.

=========================
OS Usage:
=========================
Prior to Prescott they used to use the halt instruction but halt sleepers can only be
woken up using IPI from another core which is a waste. mwait users can be woken up
using memory writes and interrupts happening on that core.

